  message: "RE-SCOPED and demoted P1 -> P3; root cause corrected from analyzer-traversal\nbug to grammar parse failure plus undisclosed degradation.\n\nHOW: adversarial premise-check (2026-08-01) during the full-corpus leverage\nreview, then re-verified by hand before this update. Probe (production\ngrammar tree_sitter_kotlin 1.1.0):\n  - filed two-one-liner fixture: parse tree = single ERROR node, zero\n    class_declaration children; analyze_kotlin -> [('f','function')] --\n    symptom reproduces byte-identically.\n  - same three-type content MULTILINE: has_error=False, all 6 symbols correct\n    (2 classes + 1 interface, methods owner-qualified).\n  - single one-liner: has_error=True yet correct output (grammar recovery\n    succeeds at multiplicity 1) -- matches the filing's own \"has_error is a\n    red herring\" observation, now explained by recovery capacity, not by\n    tree correctness.\nThe filing's \"tree-sitter produces the correct tree\" was checked against a\nnon-production grammar (fwcd node vocabulary 'type_identifier'; production\ntree_sitter_kotlin 1.1.0 uses 'identifier'). Instrument mismatch -- L10/L50\nspecies: the measurement, not the code, carried the error.\n\nCONSEQUENCES:\n  - kotlin.py:822 dispatch needs NO fix; do not touch it for this item.\n  - WI-jubag is NOT blocked on this item (type symbols exist for normally\n    formatted Kotlin).\n  - The interface-dispatch parity gate's kotlin fixture uses the failing\n    one-liner style and its hole text cites the refuted premise -- reformat\n    and re-measure (fix path 3 in the description).\n  - The structural gap (silent wrong output from ERROR-collapsed trees,\n    cross-language) is filed as\n    INV-sukan-salun-lariz-japut-pavag-kadol-norot-vudig.\n\nDemotion rationale: population = one-liner-style files only; analyzer correct\nfor realistic formatting; nothing downstream is blocked. P1 evidence was an\nartifact of the fixture style."  # 32db
